WEBVTT

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:07.020
Finally...

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:10.480
Number sixteen,

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.820
representing Kyoto, Kitauji High School.

00:01:55.150 --> 00:01:59.260
<b>Kita High Festival 
Concert Band Concert</b>

00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:31.870
It's thanks to the teachers, guardians,

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:36.020
and all of you that we can do what we do.

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:37.800
Thank you very much.

00:02:40.990 --> 00:02:43.450
The National Concert Band Competition

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:46.530
will begin at the end of October, in Nagoya.

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:55.610
We hope to continue working hard, so we 
can bring home more good news.

00:02:56.350 --> 00:02:59.650
Now, for our final piece, "Gakuen Tengoku."

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:22.300
<i>We, the Kitauji High School Concert Band,</i>

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:24.930
<i>earned gold at the Kansai Competition.</i>

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:27.640
<i>We're set to compete at the Nationals.</i>

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:34.190
<i>Episode 6 
Rainy Conductor</i>

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:35.690
<b>Class 1-3</b>

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:35.690
<b>Cake Set</b>

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:40.240
No one's showing up.

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:43.740
Maid cafés are kind of passé.

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:45.900
Don't do that, you two.

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:48.320
You have to keep smiling.

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:49.640
Ready, and...

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:57.000
Oh, yeah! Let's do something 
showier to attract people!

00:03:57.530 --> 00:04:00.950
Café at class 1-3!

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:00.950
<b>Cake Set 500 Yen 
Coffee 100 Yen</b>

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:03.910
Please come visit...

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:06.350
We have delicious cakes!

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:08.970
People look, but no one's coming.

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:11.980
Maybe an "Aggressive Maid Café" is a bad idea.

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:14.480
If we get people like this,
it'll be a miracle.

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:17.900
I'm hoping for a miracle...

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:22.820
I'd like to have tea. May I see 
a menu, waitress-san?

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:24.700
Here it is, the miracle!

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:27.830
That's so much better!

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:30.360
A shame. It looked good on you.

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:34.060
No, it didn't. On Midori-chan, maybe...

00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:35.960
Are those two still on shift?

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:39.860
Some kids are home sick,
so they're filling in.

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:40.630
I see.

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:42.760
Hey, where should we go?

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:46.050
Though it'll have to be quick, 
since I have to work, too.

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:49.310
Then, let's go to the cat café 
Midori-chan recommended.

00:04:49.310 --> 00:04:52.470
I thought you couldn't bring animals in.

00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:54.100
Yeah, so...

00:04:55.970 --> 00:04:57.350
Stuffed animals.

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:58.770
That makes sense.

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:01.470
Want to go somewhere else?

00:05:01.470 --> 00:05:02.780
Yeah.

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:03.780
<b>Class 2-2 and 2-3 Joint
Strawberry Whip</b>

00:05:05.230 --> 00:05:06.510
Hello.

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:07.320
Hi.

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:09.420
Uh, well...

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:11.240
Here.

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:14.350
That's so Yoroizuka-senpai.

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:17.310
She isn't cut out for hospitality work.

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:19.170
What is this?!

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:21.900
You're obviously messing with me.

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:23.380
No, we aren't.

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:26.510
I don't remember ordering the 
Leaning Tower of Pisa!

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:31.510
This is our specialty strawberry crêpe, ma'am.

00:05:32.340 --> 00:05:33.770
It's special service.

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:36.480
I hope you enjoy it.

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:38.230
Fine...

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:40.150
Challenge accepted!

00:05:40.550 --> 00:05:42.690
Those two sure are close.

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:44.300
Nozomi-senpai?

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:45.190
Welcome.

00:05:45.550 --> 00:05:47.180
Do you want one of those, Nozomi?

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:50.300
Thanks, but I'll pass.

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:51.740
Want one of these?

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:54.690
Wait, aren't those orders?

00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:56.320
Those two are really close, too.

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:56.260
We can make more.

00:05:56.260 --> 00:05:57.280
Jeez.

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:58.980
Where should we go next?

00:05:58.980 --> 00:06:00.320
Let's see...

00:06:00.970 --> 00:06:02.710
Hey, they have a play.

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:04.550
<i>Undine</i>, apparently.

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:07.120
It's starting in ten, though.

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:08.060
Shuichi?

00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:09.300
Oh... Right.

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:11.890
Yuko-senpai finished it.

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:15.530
I'm getting heartburn, just thinking about it.

00:06:15.530 --> 00:06:16.430
Yo.

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:17.510
Hello.

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:19.280
Hello.

00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:22.500
Wasn't this all a lot of trouble, 
given your club workload?

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:24.590
Well, you know...

00:06:24.590 --> 00:06:25.430
Yeah.

00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:29.200
We'll help you with the club.

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:30.570
Let's work hard.

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:32.120
Thank you.

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:35.420
Oh, yeah. Isn't Taki-sensei with you?

00:06:35.420 --> 00:06:38.370
He was until just now, but...

00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:42.250
Wow, he's being swarmed!

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:45.570
It appears he's made new fans 
since the Kansai Competition.

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:49.050
Well, it isn't like anyone can see his 
true personality, just by how he looks.

00:06:49.790 --> 00:06:50.930
So true.

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:53.050
Reina!

00:06:53.320 --> 00:06:54.680
You told her?

00:06:55.480 --> 00:06:57.140
About Taki-kun?

00:06:58.920 --> 00:06:59.600
No.

00:07:00.930 --> 00:07:01.690
Reina...

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:04.370
You looked so sharp in your tailcoat—

00:07:04.370 --> 00:07:05.390
Taki-sensei.

00:07:07.240 --> 00:07:10.530
Hashimoto-sensei is
waiting for you over there.

00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:14.220
I know the feeling,
but you can't lie like that!

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:16.610
It was true that they
were waiting in the hall.

00:07:16.610 --> 00:07:20.680
They weren't really waiting. 
It was more like watching.

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:23.760
Of course I can't tell her.

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:24.670
What?

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:27.590
Oh, nothing.

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:30.890
<i>I wonder if Taki-sensei knows...</i>

00:07:31.330 --> 00:07:33.520
<i>About Reina's feelings.</i>

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:39.980
<i>I wonder how Reina felt.</i>

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:43.540
<i>What was going through her mind when she...</i>

00:07:43.970 --> 00:07:44.650
Kumiko!

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:48.660
Are you all right?

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:51.490
<b>Come to Class 3-2</b>

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:52.900
Wait, do you know them?

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:54.660
I don't think so.

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:56.800
Did I scare you?

00:07:56.800 --> 00:07:58.040
Kaori-senpai?

00:07:58.040 --> 00:08:00.100
What's with the suit?

00:07:58.040 --> 00:08:05.670
<b>Come to Class 3-2</b>

00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:02.350
I'm in charge of marketing.

00:08:02.350 --> 00:08:04.860
Our class is putting on a dance performance.

00:08:04.860 --> 00:08:05.980
Wow!

00:08:05.980 --> 00:08:08.750
Oh, yeah. Have you gone to Asuka's place?

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:10.340
No, not yet...

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:14.010
You should check it out. 
It's supposed to be pretty fun.

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:15.870
Asuka-senpai's, huh?

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:17.350
Should we go?

00:08:17.350 --> 00:08:20.390
Okay, guys, have fun!

00:08:17.350 --> 00:08:20.390
<b>Come to Class 3-2</b>

00:08:21.030 --> 00:08:22.390
She's all in.

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:24.480
I'm going back to my class now.

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:26.690
I'm supposed to be there until 2:30.

00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:27.800
Come visit.

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:29.050
Okay.

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:31.320
Let's see, Asuka-senpai...

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:34.910
Welcome, my lost little lamb!

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:37.080
You look good in that.

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:38.400
I know, right?

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:41.440
You're the only one who gets it...

00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:43.710
What are the others doing?

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:46.280
We're all fortune tellers, obviously.

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:47.600
Isn't that too many?

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:49.440
Hey, want me to read your fortune?

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:50.550
No, thank you.

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:52.090
Your future holds—

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:54.170
No, thank you!

00:08:54.170 --> 00:08:55.830
You're no fun.

00:08:55.830 --> 00:08:58.080
You've gotta get in the mood.

00:08:58.080 --> 00:09:01.600
Like, "Huh? Then tell me about my love life!"

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:05.060
What do you know about me, Asuka-senpai?

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:07.240
Hey, I didn't give you permission to look!

00:09:07.240 --> 00:09:08.190
Pervert.

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:11.380
I'm not telling you how to get bigger boobs!

00:09:11.380 --> 00:09:12.780
I don't need your help.

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:15.240
Jeez, Asuka, shut up.

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:18.660
It's getting busy inside. Hurry and help out.

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:21.040
See, you got in trouble.

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:28.130
You indignant underclassman, 
may a ghost curse you!

00:09:29.050 --> 00:09:30.380
Asuka!

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:31.750
<b>Oh! So Scary</b>

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:31.750
<b>Haunted House</b>

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:34.450
Uh...

00:09:34.450 --> 00:09:35.840
Haunted house.

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:38.180
This is Reina's class?

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:40.470
No, no...

00:09:40.870 --> 00:09:43.120
I can't handle stuff like this.

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:44.600
Reina...

00:09:47.300 --> 00:09:48.710
That scared me!

00:09:51.260 --> 00:09:52.540
Takigawa-kun?

00:09:54.670 --> 00:09:55.990
What a wuss.

00:09:58.600 --> 00:09:59.870
What?

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:01.150
Nothing.

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:05.370
Quit making weird noises!

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:08.790
B-B-But... My flashlight went out!

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:10.680
It's part of the trick.

00:10:10.680 --> 00:10:12.210
Let's hurry up and find the exit.

00:10:12.210 --> 00:10:12.920
Wait!

00:10:15.930 --> 00:10:17.010
What?

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:20.260
I can't deal with this stuff.

00:10:20.740 --> 00:10:23.690
I'd appreciate if you
wouldn't get too ahead...

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:27.030
It's intricate.

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:29.370
Am I walking too fast?

00:10:29.370 --> 00:10:31.310
No, you're fine.

00:10:31.670 --> 00:10:33.490
The competition was awesome.

00:10:33.490 --> 00:10:35.860
Yeah, everyone was really good.

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:37.020
Yeah.

00:10:39.310 --> 00:10:43.660
Hey, Kumiko, at the next competition—

00:10:44.380 --> 00:10:47.330
I've been waiting for you!

00:10:47.330 --> 00:10:48.410
Wh-What?

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:51.270
Reina...

00:10:52.680 --> 00:10:54.920
You're laughing too much.

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:56.300
Sorry...

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:58.930
But the way you and Tsukamoto reacted...

00:10:58.930 --> 00:11:01.690
You were way too scary as a ghost.

00:11:01.690 --> 00:11:04.010
But you just bumped into each other?

00:11:04.010 --> 00:11:05.310
What? Who?

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:06.530
Tsukamoto.

00:11:07.230 --> 00:11:10.190
Stop it! Obviously, it was a coincidence!

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:11.270
I see.

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:12.440
Yeah.

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:14.400
All right, then.

00:11:18.590 --> 00:11:20.230
It's so windy.

00:11:20.230 --> 00:11:21.360
Are you all right?

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:23.530
I heard a typhoon's coming.

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:24.840
Yeah.

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:28.470
I'm glad the school festival wasn't canceled.

00:11:28.470 --> 00:11:30.320
We all worked so hard to prepare.

00:11:30.320 --> 00:11:33.540
Yes, but I heard school might 
be closed tomorrow.

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:34.540
Really?

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:35.420
Yes!

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:38.040
Let me guess. You haven't
studied for the quiz.

00:11:38.040 --> 00:11:39.450
No...

00:11:39.450 --> 00:11:41.450
I was busy.

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:46.600
Starting tomorrow, it's back to practice.

00:11:47.780 --> 00:11:48.780
Yeah.

00:11:50.420 --> 00:11:51.890
It feels weird.

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:55.940
It's already fall, and we're still 
practicing for competition.

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:57.400
Weird, huh?

00:11:57.400 --> 00:11:58.380
Yeah.

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:09.870
<i>Just like that, the typhoon's winds 
blew away our nonchalance.</i>

00:12:09.870 --> 00:12:12.910
<i>By the time it began to rain that night,</i>

00:12:12.910 --> 00:12:15.630
<i>we were back to our everyday routine.</i>

00:12:19.550 --> 00:12:21.390
It's way too broad.

00:12:26.880 --> 00:12:28.310
Onee-chan?

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:30.460
Jeez, it's all wet.

00:12:35.200 --> 00:12:36.020
Come on...

00:12:36.320 --> 00:12:39.820
The bath's ready. Get in 
before you catch a cold.

00:12:40.180 --> 00:12:41.160
Mamiko?

00:12:41.580 --> 00:12:42.620
Mom...

00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:43.490
Yes?

00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:46.410
I think I'm going to drop out of college.

00:12:56.490 --> 00:13:00.500
<i>Large, powerful Typhoon 20 
is advancing northeast</i>

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:01.170
<b>Unavailable</b>

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:04.760
<i>at 25 km/h, bringing strong 
rainstorms along the way.</i>

00:13:05.520 --> 00:13:09.890
<i>Please beware of strong winds and high waves.</i>

00:13:10.390 --> 00:13:12.740
<i>Please stay indoors as much as possible.</i>

00:13:14.230 --> 00:13:18.850
<b>The wind's getting stronger 

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:23.890
<b>School's Canceled 

00:13:24.830 --> 00:13:27.320
Stuff, I guess...

00:13:27.960 --> 00:13:30.240
I think I'm going to drop out of college.

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:34.750
How many times must I ask you to tell us why?

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:35.910
Honey...

00:13:35.910 --> 00:13:38.960
I told you, I don't want to go anymore.

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:42.780
Fine. I'll talk to you more when I get home.

00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:47.180
See you.

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:48.010
Yeah.

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:53.110
You don't need to tell anyone about this.

00:13:53.110 --> 00:13:54.680
I know.

00:13:57.080 --> 00:13:59.690
Onee-chan, you're quitting school?

00:14:00.510 --> 00:14:04.460
After how much you nagged me 
to study, you're dropping out?

00:14:05.650 --> 00:14:07.520
You're doing nothing but club work.

00:14:07.520 --> 00:14:11.080
You'd better start studying now, or you 
won't make it into university.

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:14.070
What's the point of continuing concert band,

00:14:14.070 --> 00:14:15.660
when you don't even plan 
to go to music school?!

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:16.980
Why?

00:14:16.980 --> 00:14:21.290
Weren't you studying so you could attend 
a good college and land a good job?

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:23.440
That was all pointless if you quit!

00:14:24.930 --> 00:14:26.800
It's none of your business.

00:14:29.770 --> 00:14:31.970
Wait, where do you think you're going?

00:14:31.970 --> 00:14:33.060
Shopping.

00:14:36.370 --> 00:14:38.960
<i>It wasn't that I had anywhere to go.</i>

00:14:38.960 --> 00:14:42.500
<i>I just didn't want to stay at home.</i>

00:14:42.500 --> 00:14:44.610
<i>I couldn't take the heavy mood.</i>

00:14:50.510 --> 00:14:55.080
<i>I had a feeling that if I stayed any longer, 
I'd get in a fight with my sister.</i>

00:14:58.910 --> 00:15:00.670
<i>Taki-sensei...</i>

00:15:04.590 --> 00:15:05.720
Oumae-san?

00:15:06.990 --> 00:15:09.510
You shouldn't be out on a day like this.

00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:11.930
Sorry. I wanted to take a walk.

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:13.600
In this rain?

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:16.020
Um, I like the rain.

00:15:16.440 --> 00:15:18.580
Will you be okay in the rain, Sensei?

00:15:18.580 --> 00:15:20.570
Yes, I drove.

00:15:20.570 --> 00:15:22.600
I don't like typhoons, though.

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:24.480
My shoes are soaked.

00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:28.340
Do you often come to this flower shop?

00:15:28.340 --> 00:15:29.730
Well, sometimes.

00:15:30.420 --> 00:15:33.630
They were supposed to be closed 
today for the typhoon,

00:15:33.630 --> 00:15:35.910
but they were kind enough to 
make something for me.

00:15:36.430 --> 00:15:38.490
I may have asked them for too much.

00:15:40.150 --> 00:15:42.580
But you must be a little happy.

00:15:43.620 --> 00:15:45.250
With school being canceled.

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:47.140
Oh, yes.

00:15:47.140 --> 00:15:51.580
When I was a student, I was always 
excited when there was a typhoon.

00:15:51.580 --> 00:15:54.260
It usually passed by morning, though.

00:15:54.260 --> 00:15:55.410
You're right!

00:15:55.410 --> 00:15:57.760
School's rarely canceled.

00:15:57.760 --> 00:15:59.420
You sure sound serious.

00:15:59.420 --> 00:16:00.660
N-No...

00:16:00.660 --> 00:16:01.350
Yeah.

00:16:01.350 --> 00:16:03.690
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:16:03.690 --> 00:16:06.530
No, sorry to ask it of you on a day like this.

00:16:06.530 --> 00:16:07.640
It's fine.

00:16:07.970 --> 00:16:09.430
Your daughter?

00:16:09.430 --> 00:16:10.720
My student.

00:16:10.720 --> 00:16:12.610
She just happened to pass by.

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:13.700
I see.

00:16:14.110 --> 00:16:17.690
Of course. You're still young.

00:16:17.690 --> 00:16:19.040
I'll be off.

00:16:19.440 --> 00:16:21.710
Exact change, thank you.

00:16:23.420 --> 00:16:25.170
Your ring—

00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:30.840
Today is a special day.

00:16:32.620 --> 00:16:36.300
<i>His voice was so kind,
it almost gave me chills.</i>

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:39.640
<i>But it was also strict, as if to 
discourage further prying.</i>

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:45.170
I'm heading home now.

00:16:45.170 --> 00:16:46.890
Are you sure?

00:16:46.890 --> 00:16:48.910
You should wait until it eases up.

00:16:48.910 --> 00:16:50.950
O-Oh, I like the rain.

00:16:51.600 --> 00:16:52.700
Oumae-san!

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:55.740
This is no good.

00:16:57.170 --> 00:16:58.980
I have stuff in the back seat.

00:16:58.980 --> 00:16:59.830
Sit in front.

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:00.740
Okay.

00:17:00.740 --> 00:17:02.820
Here, use this.

00:17:02.820 --> 00:17:04.750
Thank you very much.

00:17:35.260 --> 00:17:38.450
I heard Hashimoto-sensei told you a little.

00:17:41.010 --> 00:17:42.420
He was married.

00:17:42.420 --> 00:17:45.330
But she passed away five years ago.

00:17:45.710 --> 00:17:48.460
Yes, just a little bit.

00:17:48.820 --> 00:17:54.670
After camp, he apologized to me, 
saying he let it slip.

00:17:54.670 --> 00:17:56.330
He's so awkward.

00:17:57.130 --> 00:18:02.000
Is the person in that photo your wife?

00:18:04.630 --> 00:18:08.080
Sorry. I shouldn't have asked.

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:09.360
It's fine.

00:18:09.710 --> 00:18:12.060
Sorry to make things difficult for you.

00:18:12.060 --> 00:18:14.690
I'm not upset or anything.

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:15.660
Which way?

00:18:16.850 --> 00:18:18.160
Left.

00:18:22.190 --> 00:18:24.080
As you suspected,

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:27.160
that's my wife in the picture.

00:18:27.520 --> 00:18:29.300
At college, she was in my year.

00:18:29.300 --> 00:18:34.250
Hashimoto-sensei and my wife were both 
students at Kitauji High School, too.

00:18:34.250 --> 00:18:35.890
I never knew.

00:18:35.890 --> 00:18:36.840
Yes.

00:18:36.840 --> 00:18:39.140
My father was the adviser at the time.

00:18:39.140 --> 00:18:41.430
Apparently, they made it to the Nationals.

00:18:41.430 --> 00:18:42.510
"Apparently"?

00:18:42.510 --> 00:18:45.840
I was rebellious back then.

00:18:45.840 --> 00:18:49.280
I don't know too much, but from 
what my wife told me,

00:18:49.280 --> 00:18:54.440
although they made the Nationals, they never 
won gold during their high school years.

00:18:54.440 --> 00:18:56.900
So, even after she became ill,

00:18:56.900 --> 00:18:59.790
she said that she would become a teacher,

00:18:59.790 --> 00:19:02.740
and lead her alma mater to gold.

00:19:09.290 --> 00:19:12.790
<i>Taki-sensei didn't say any more.</i>

00:19:13.370 --> 00:19:18.300
<i>He probably didn't want to force 
his personal issues on us.</i>

00:19:18.720 --> 00:19:20.550
What is this?

00:19:20.550 --> 00:19:22.300
That isn't good.

00:19:24.590 --> 00:19:27.190
<i>But he deeply wished for it...</i>

00:19:27.190 --> 00:19:28.680
<i>To win gold at the Nationals.</i>

00:19:29.180 --> 00:19:32.660
<i>For Kitauji High School to win 
gold at the Nationals!</i>

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:39.400
Okay...

00:19:45.370 --> 00:19:46.970
Yoroizuka-senpai...

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:49.470
Good morning.

00:19:49.470 --> 00:19:50.570
Morning.

00:19:50.570 --> 00:19:52.630
You're early, as always.

00:19:52.630 --> 00:19:54.800
I don't want Nozomi to laugh at me.

00:19:54.800 --> 00:19:56.790
And I have to make up for yesterday.

00:19:57.670 --> 00:20:00.170
I'm just glad my quiz was canceled.

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:01.970
But apparently, it'll be next week.

00:20:02.490 --> 00:20:03.490
Reina!

00:20:03.490 --> 00:20:05.130
You're here earlier than usual.

00:20:05.130 --> 00:20:07.470
Yeah, I felt a little eager.

00:20:07.470 --> 00:20:09.430
Kumiko-chan! Reina-chan!

00:20:09.760 --> 00:20:11.940
Midori-chan's here early, too.

00:20:13.290 --> 00:20:17.570
I guess now that we're here, we all 
want gold at the Nationals.

00:20:17.570 --> 00:20:19.450
That's it! That's exactly it!

00:20:19.450 --> 00:20:23.410
Let's keep practicing and get even better.

00:20:23.410 --> 00:20:27.080
I hope we get a lot of good new students.

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:28.520
New students?

00:20:28.520 --> 00:20:29.800
Of course we will.

00:20:29.800 --> 00:20:31.660
Taki-sensei is here.

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:34.460
Good teachers attract good students.

00:20:34.460 --> 00:20:36.050
Good students like you?

00:20:36.050 --> 00:20:37.330
I won't deny it.

00:20:40.230 --> 00:20:41.500
What's wrong?

00:20:41.500 --> 00:20:42.740
Those flowers...

00:20:43.580 --> 00:20:45.600
Italian Whites, right?

00:20:45.600 --> 00:20:46.930
Italian Whites?

00:20:46.930 --> 00:20:48.940
What about them?

00:20:48.940 --> 00:20:51.610
O-Oh, they're just pretty.

00:20:51.610 --> 00:20:54.350
I know! I love them, too.

00:20:54.700 --> 00:20:57.340
Their meaning in floriography 
is romantic, as well.

00:20:57.340 --> 00:20:58.440
Floriography?

00:20:58.440 --> 00:20:59.150
Yes.

00:20:59.150 --> 00:21:02.400
Italian Whites' meaning in floriography

00:21:02.400 --> 00:21:04.810
is "I'll always be thinking of you."

00:21:05.850 --> 00:21:07.180
<i>"I'll always</i>

00:21:08.450 --> 00:21:10.200
<i>be thinking of you."</i>

00:21:16.400 --> 00:21:17.840
I'm so glad

00:21:18.550 --> 00:21:21.010
Taki-sensei is our adviser.

00:21:22.750 --> 00:21:24.930
Of course you are. Let's go.

00:21:24.930 --> 00:21:26.720
The Nationals are waiting.

00:21:26.720 --> 00:21:27.820
Yeah!

00:21:27.820 --> 00:21:31.690
The Nationals are waiting for us!

00:21:36.190 --> 00:21:39.070
<i>"I hope we get a lot of good new students."</i>

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:41.690
<i>I didn't mean much when I said it.</i>

00:21:42.110 --> 00:21:46.270
<i>But it also implied that the 
third-years would be retiring.</i>

00:22:01.860 --> 00:22:05.790
<i>And the next piece begins.</i>

00:22:05.920 --> 00:22:09.930
<b>To Be Continued</b>
